# /public/build is deliberately NOT ignored. The production host (BigRock shared
# hosting) has no Node — `node -v` and `npm -v` are both "command not found" — so the
# compiled CSS/JS cannot be built there. Ignoring it meant a fresh `git clone` on the
# server had no `public/build/manifest.json` and every page died with
# ViteManifestNotFoundException until someone remembered to scp the folder across by
# hand. Committing the build output makes a deploy `git pull` and nothing else.
# Run `npm run build` and commit the result whenever CSS or JS changes.
